+ * CUDA grammar. `__launch_bounds__(...)` before a declarator makes the
+ * attribute parse as the function name, and `k<<<grid, block>>>(args)` parses
+ * as shift expressions, so the launch carries no CALLS edge. Mask these CUDA
+ * extensions with spaces (length- and newline-preserving, so every node offset
+ * and row/column still maps onto the original text) before parsing. A launch
+ * then parses as the ordinary call `k(args)`.
